                    {
                        "sense_id": "820a9ae0-fc59-3c24-bc03-d870e1e9e9bf",
                        "entry_id": "081d4d29-9eee-3d13-970a-a8f857356369",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to cover with moss, to stuff or caulk with moss"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "imperfective",
                            "regional"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8bd2ae9-4891-400a-a903-94ee3094fa6f",
                                "sense_id": "820a9ae0-fc59-3c24-bc03-d870e1e9e9bf",
                                "text": "В старину́ в Росси́и деревя́нные дома́ и амба́ры мши́ли, то есть конопа́тили мхом, что́бы зимо́й в них бы́ло тепло́.",
                                "translation": "In the old days in Russia houses and barns were mossed, that is, caulked with moss, to make them warm in winter.",
                                "english": "In the old days in Russia houses and barns were mossed, that is, caulked with moss, to make them warm in winter."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
